    "body": "From https://www.ietf.org/slides/slides-agews-paper-device-based-age-verification-00.pdf\n\n> When inserting a meta tag to the document, if the \"name\" attribute is \"rating\" and\nthe \"content\" attribute is \"RTA-5042-1996-1400-1577-RTA\" or \"adult\", and if the\nbrowser is configured by the host platform to restrict adult content, the operation\nmust fail and the browser may redirect the user to an error page.\n\n> Maybe there's an existing ontology with broad support that could be referenced, instead of inventing something anew.\n\nThis is an existing ontology, as far as I can tell.\n\nhttps://developers.google.com/search/docs/specialty/explicit/guidelines#add-metadata\nhttps://www.rtalabel.org/?content=howto#top",
